--   **The geometry of the `A` axis steps** (round-six regime).
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6AIL10`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.axA_geom (P : Prm) (hP : P.Ok) : ∃ n₁ : ℕ, ∀ n, n₁ ≤ n → ∀ src : ℕ → ℕ,
--       SrcOK6 P n src → ∀ D : ℕ, dP6 P n = D + 1 → ∀ k ≤ D,
--       1 ≤ HA6 P n ∧ 0 < tF6 P n k / (16 * HA6 P n) ∧
--       tF6 P n k = tF6 P n k / (16 * HA6 P n) * 8 * (2 * HA6 P n) ∧
--       J6A.WA (pP6 P n) (αN6 P n) (HA6 P n) ≤ src k ∧ src k ≤ tF6 P n k ∧
--       2 * J6A.WA (pP6 P n) (αN6 P n) (HA6 P n) * tF6 P n k ≤ 16 * HA6 P n * src k ∧
--       2 * J6A.WA (pP6 P n) (αN6 P n) (HA6 P n) ≤ 8 * HA6 P n ∧
--       2 ^ (Nat.log 2 (sWidth (pP6 P n) (αN6 P n)) + 3) = 8 * HA6 P n ∧
--       0 < preT P n D k ∧ 0 < postT P n D k
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** A lines, IL side 10: the axis geometry and the kernel row facts
--
--   * **`axA_geom`**: in the round-six regime, for every axis `k ≤ D` (`H = HA6`, `t = t_k`,
--     `s = src k`, `W = WA p α H`): `1 ≤ H`, `0 < t/16H`, `t = t/16H · 8 · 2H`, `W ≤ s ≤ t`,
--     `2Wt ≤ 16Hs`, `2W ≤ 8H`, `2^(⌊log₂ m⌋+3) = 8H`, `0 < preT`, `0 < postT`;
--   * **`gK_length`**: the kernel keeps a row of length `8H` (when `2W ≤ 8H`);
--   * **`aKerL_AB`** / **`gK_GB`**: the kernel output bound `AB (Kc ((w2+bk) Kr (Ka X0 + 1) + 1) + 1)`,
--     hence `GB (pk + 1)` under the `aK_runs` condition `he3`.
